title: Two Million Unemployed
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and unemployment >= 7.5 and unemployment_2m = 0
new-page: true
on-arrival: unemployment_2m = 1; thatcher_rating -= 3; wet_dissent += 5; rebellion += 1
face-image: img/events/two_million.jpg

= Two Million Unemployed

The unemployment count has passed two million for the first time since the 1930s. The papers print the same dole-queue photographs we used in 1978, with the caption reversed.

@three_million
title: Three Million Unemployed
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and unemployment >= 11.5 and unemployment_3m = 0
new-page: true
on-arrival: unemployment_3m = 1; thatcher_rating -= 4; wet_dissent += 6; rebellion += 2; c2_con -= 2; de_con -= 2
face-image: img/events/three_million.jpg

= Three Million Unemployed

One in eight of the workforce is now out of work. In parts of Merseyside, Clydeside and the North East it is worse than one in five. The Church of England, the CBI and the TUC unite to demand a change of course.
